    "summary": "Turn 4: the previously accepted Candidate (9ec6e94d662d478fb726520343d9acdd, pending_work) is resolved as explained by source investigation rather than by execution. Sourced result: handlePrepareReply sets subCase = 4 only inside the branch at epaxos/epaxos.go:1272, whose guard (preAcceptCount >= r.Replica.SlowQuorumSize()-1 && !lb.leaderResponded && allEqual) is textually identical to the preceding sub-case 3 guard at epaxos/epaxos.go:1269; when the first is false the second is false, so subCase = 4 never executes. bcastTryPreAccept is called only under subCase == 4 (epaxos/epaxos.go:1304-1306), so handleTryPreAccept, handleTryPreAcceptReply, lb.tryingToPreAccept, deferMap and the inert notInQuorum guard are all dead code. Therefore no TryPreAccept defer cycle can arise and the inert guard cannot cause a recovery stall; the original observation (lb.possibleQuorum initialized all-false and only ever assigned false at epaxos/epaxos.go:1445-1446; the notInQuorum loop testing the constant lb.possibleQuorum[tpar.AcceptorId] instead of [q] at epaxos/epaxos.go:1461) stands but has no observable consequence here, so no defect is claimed. The submission uses action=explained for that candidate, with feedback refs to the candidate, B-PREPARE-REPLY-LEADER, B-TPA-REPLY-LEADER and F-RECOVERY-DECISION, and it preserves a distinct open question rather than over-claiming: whether recovery is complete without the TryPreAccept conflict check for instances pre-accepted by fewer than SlowQuorumSize()-1 replicas, plus the untouched A1 fast-path and A2 ballot/authority lines. Note: the two prior rejections were purely a reply-format issue (the turn harness parses the final message as exactly this JSON envelope); this reply is emitted as that envelope only. Preflight validation returns valid=true; formal acceptance and any execution remain the controller's."
